      "message": "Returning early at lines 780 or 785 leaves `layerPromise` (`this.initLayers()` at line 778) un-awaited without `.catch(() \u003d\u003e {})`: if `this.path` becomes `undefined` on navigation/disconnect while `getPreferences()` is in flight, `assertIsDefined(this.path, \u0027path\u0027)` at line 715 rejects unhandled, and a slow `initLayers()` can still overwrite `this.layers` and clear `this.coverageRanges \u003d []` for the newer reload. Similarly, `loadDiffAssets(diff)` mutates `this.baseImage`/`this.revisionImage` inside `.then(...)` (lines 1237–1240) before line 785\u0027s `reloadId` check runs. Consider attaching `layerPromise.catch(() \u003d\u003e {})` and guarding state writes in `initLayers` and `loadDiffAssets` with `reloadId \u003d\u003d\u003d this.reloadGeneration`.",
