      "message": "Two boundary cases in `startsNewTopLevelCommandInDeclBody`: (1) it returns `false` on `/-!`, `@[`, `parseStandaloneModifiersLine` (`unsafe`, `partial`, etc.), and (when `!isTypeDecl`) `/--`, so in `theorem clean : 1 + 1 \u003d 2 :\u003d rfl\\n\\n  unsafe\\n  def bad : Nat :\u003d 0`, `clean` absorbs `unsafe` into its proof body while `bad` loses `hygiene.isUnsafe`; and (2) `dirKw \u003d\u003d\u003d \u0027deriving\u0027` is only exempted when `isTypeDecl` (splitting valid `def`/`abbrev ...\\n  deriving BEq, Repr`, whereas only `deriving instance` is top-level) and `afterKw.startsWith(\u0027:\u0027)` splits parameterized `where` members like `prefix x :\u003d ...` or `syntax (n : Nat) : String`. Consider treating declaration prefixes as command boundaries, allowing non-`instance` `deriving` on any declaration, and exempting parameterized member definitions inside `where` blocks.",
